{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Independent non-author documentation review receipt for exact authored revision a4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21. Reviewer session /root@2026-09-10-resume did not author the remediation. The review inspected every declared block against immutable base 88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684, confirmed the 19-path parent-to-final AST and directive oracle, and found zero documentation-policy punctuation or banned-term patterns in added prose.\n\nstable_block_id\tbefore_citation\tfinal_citation\tpreserved_contract_or_consumer\tdirectives_exact\tbefore_words\tafter_words\tsemantic-preservation\tbloat-removal\treviewer_session\ntests/_bank_observer.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_bank_observer.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_bank_observer.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Shared bookkeeping for the completion-banking behavioral eval. ``make_observed_upsert`` wraps ``CriterionBank.upsert`` without narrowing its keyword-only contract, records the first durable write by either the model or bounded fallback, and excludes ``seeded=True`` pre-run cache state. ``make_response_counting_wrap`` and ``bounded_bank_gaps`` measure distinct ``ctx.run_step`` evidence responses where a governed tool actually executed. Batched reads make calls the wrong unit. Synthetic steering notices do not count, while an executed call carrying a bounded-fallback notice does. The provider-backed eval and its unit regressions share these helpers so signature, actor, and response-unit drift is caught without requiring a provider run.\tPASS\t300\t95\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_bank_observer.py#D:make_observed_upsert\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_bank_observer.py#D:make_observed_upsert\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_bank_observer.py#D:make_observed_upsert\tpytest and maintainers of make_observed_upsert. Preserves Wrap ``CriterionBank.upsert`` and record each criterion's first durable bank write. Model and bounded-fallback writes both count. ``seeded=True`` cache seeds do not. All inspected and future keyword-only arguments are forwarded unchanged to ``original_upsert``.\tPASS\t98\t34\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_bank_observer.py#D:make_response_counting_wrap\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_bank_observer.py#D:make_response_counting_wrap\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_bank_observer.py#D:make_response_counting_wrap\tpytest and maintainers of make_response_counting_wrap. Preserves Wrap the original evidence policy and count distinct executed evidence responses. Governed calls add ``ctx.run_step`` unless the policy returned an unexecuted synthetic notice. Calls with an appended bounded-fallback notice did execute and count. Because the fallback banks inside the policy before this outer counter runs, its snapshot may be one response low, which is conservative for the ``<= max_gap`` oracle.\tPASS\t124\t60\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_bank_observer.py#D:bounded_bank_gaps\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_bank_observer.py#D:bounded_bank_gaps\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_bank_observer.py#D:bounded_bank_gaps\tpytest and maintainers of bounded_bank_gaps. Preserves Require every criterion's first durable bank within bounded response gaps. ``responses_at_bank`` includes the first model or fallback write. The first point and every later delta must be at most ``max_gap``. Empty, incomplete, late, or verdict-less trials fail.\tPASS\t91\t37\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_child_diag.py#D:assert_child_ran_clean\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_child_diag.py#D:assert_child_ran_clean\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_child_diag.py#D:assert_child_ran_clean\tpytest and maintainers of assert_child_ran_clean. Preserves Assert that *proc* completed with an accepted code and no traceback. Check the code first because a signal-killed child can leave empty stderr and make a traceback-only oracle fail open. Rejected exits reuse :func:`child_failure_detail`. Accepted exits quote a traceback tail directly because a failed-exit preamble would be misleading. ``ok_codes`` defaults to ``(0,)`` but callers may include legitimate codes such as reconciler RESCHEDULE (75).\tPASS\t297\t64\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_child_diag.py#D:assert_child_was_not_signal_killed\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_child_diag.py#D:assert_child_was_not_signal_killed\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_child_diag.py#D:assert_child_was_not_signal_killed\tpytest and maintainers of assert_child_was_not_signal_killed. Preserves Reject signal termination without imposing a normal-exit or traceback contract. This protects absence-based oracles from empty output after a killed child. Only CPython's negative signal return codes fail. Positive ``128+N`` values remain valid normal exits. Failures reuse :func:`child_failure_detail` for consistent signal diagnostics.\tPASS\t225\t44\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_engine_path.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_engine_path.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_engine_path.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Choose the checkout's bundled engine as the tests tree's single canonical root. Non-editable installs contain both checkout and site-packages copies. Because ``sys.modules`` has one flat ``rebar_reconciler.*`` namespace, mixing them can create duplicate class identities and false ``isinstance`` results. Tests inspect, patch, and measure the checkout, and the unit shadow package already resolves there, so :func:`engine_dir` is canonical for every test binding. The runtime conftest guard checks resulting module state and a static test checks call sites. ``rebar._engine.engine_dir()`` remains correct for production subprocess launches.\tPASS\t423\t86\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_engine_path.py#D:engine_root_of\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_engine_path.py#D:engine_root_of\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_engine_path.py#D:engine_root_of\tpytest and maintainers of engine_root_of. Preserves Return the enclosing ``.../rebar/_engine`` root, or ``None`` for non-engine files. Test shadow packages may legitimately hold canonical keys. Only duplicated engine files are subject to the single-root rule.\tPASS\t51\t28\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_engine_path.py#D:_foreign_root\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_engine_path.py#D:_foreign_root\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_engine_path.py#D:_foreign_root\tpytest and maintainers of _foreign_root. Preserves Return a non-canonical engine root, caching path strings to avoid per-test resolves.\tPASS\t42\t12\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_engine_path.py#D:foreign_engine_registrations\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_engine_path.py#D:foreign_engine_registrations\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_engine_path.py#D:foreign_engine_registrations\tpytest and maintainers of foreign_engine_registrations. Preserves List canonical bindings served by a non-canonical engine copy. Sorted ``(what, path)`` pairs cover module keys and package ``__path__`` entries. Inspecting final import state catches assignments, ``setdefault``, imports, and path mutation uniformly.\tPASS\t86\t31\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_extra_guard.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_extra_guard.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_extra_guard.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Make missing Python extras fail loudly in CI instead of silently shrinking coverage. When ``REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1``, :func:`install` replaces ``pytest.importorskip`` with a strict variant because CI promises to install every test-bearing extra. Binary- and version-based ``skipif`` cases remain deliberately skippable. Keeping the guard outside ``conftest.py`` makes the same implementation directly testable without re-executing pytest configuration.\tPASS\t230\t57\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_git_counts.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_git_counts.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_git_counts.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Crash-safe Git commit counting shared by tests. Transient ``git rev-list --count`` failures can return empty stdout. Retry them, then surface Git's rc/stdout/stderr instead of an opaque ``int('')`` error. Import this root helper bare because ``tests/`` is on ``sys.path``.\tPASS\t121\t41\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_git_floor.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_git_floor.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_git_floor.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Declare and enforce rebar's Git version floor. Two-clone convergence tests require ``git merge-tree --write-tree`` (Git 2.38). Skipping them on older clients would silently remove regression coverage. The suite therefore fails loudly below the version single-sourced in ``.github/git-version-floor.txt``, which contributor docs and CI also read.\tPASS\t143\t47\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_git_upkeep.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_git_upkeep.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_git_upkeep.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Build fixture bare remotes with no background Git upkeep. By default, ``receive-pack`` may detach ``git maintenance`` after a push returns. A fixture that then copies, byte-walks, or locally clones the remote can race a repack that removes object entries. Measured unpinned local clones failed with exit 128, while pinned runs did not. rebar-owned stores already pin auto-detach behavior, but fixture remotes need their own setup. ``receive.autogc=false`` suppresses unnecessary upkeep. Both ``autoDetach`` pins force any other trigger to finish in the foreground. This removes the mutator without retries, sleeps, ignored paths, or weaker assertions. The bare-clone source sweep guards adoption, and callers import this root helper bare through the ``tests/`` path.\tPASS\t518\t112\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_git_upkeep.py#D:init_bare_remote\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_git_upkeep.py#D:init_bare_remote\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_git_upkeep.py#D:init_bare_remote\tpytest and maintainers of init_bare_remote. Preserves Create *remote* bare and apply upkeep pins before any push can reach it. *initial_branch* supplies fixtures such as ``--initial-branch=tickets`` without inviting a separate, unpinned ``git init --bare`` path.\tPASS\t77\t29\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_isolation.py#D:leak_failure_message\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_isolation.py#D:leak_failure_message\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_isolation.py#D:leak_failure_message\tpytest and maintainers of leak_failure_message. Preserves Explain newly observed REPO_ROOT entries without guessing their writer. Per-test snapshots cannot distinguish a test leak from a concurrent external write, so the message names both and leaves all files untouched for the operator to classify safely.\tPASS\t86\t37\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_isolation.py#D:head_move_failure_message\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_isolation.py#D:head_move_failure_message\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_isolation.py#D:head_move_failure_message\tpytest and maintainers of head_move_failure_message. Preserves Explain a HEAD move without attributing indistinguishable concurrent commits. Two SHA samples reveal no writer identity, so the message names test and external causes. Its destructive recovery command appears only after a warning to establish ownership first.\tPASS\t120\t37\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_isolation.py#D:working_tree_failure_message\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_isolation.py#D:working_tree_failure_message\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_isolation.py#D:working_tree_failure_message\tpytest and maintainers of working_tree_failure_message. Preserves Explain session-wide porcelain additions without guessing which process wrote them. A test leak and concurrent commit, build, or editor save are indistinguishable across the two snapshots, so the diagnostic presents both causes.\tPASS\t78\t32\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_isolation.py#C:<module>:before:LEAK_WATCH_SUBDIRS\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_isolation.py#C:<module>:before:LEAK_WATCH_SUBDIRS\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_isolation.py#C:<module>:before:LEAK_WATCH_SUBDIRS\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Watch volatile checkout state one level deep so writes inside an existing ``.rebar/`` are caught locally as well as on clean CI. Keep the scan cheap and exclude directories with legitimate per-test churn (``.git/``, ``.tickets-tracker/``, and ``.venv/``).\tPASS\t86\t37\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_isolation.py#C:<module>:before:GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_isolation.py#C:<module>:before:GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_isolation.py#C:<module>:before:GIT_PROBE_ATTEMPTS\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Re-sample timed-out read-only probes. One starved sample under xdist is not evidence of a repository leak. Retries add no sleep because each timeout is already backoff and tests may patch ``time.sleep``. The final ``TimeoutExpired`` propagates so a persistent inability to sample still fails loudly.\tPASS\t152\t45\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_jira_shape_contract.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_jira_shape_contract.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_jira_shape_contract.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Shared return-shape contract for ``AcliClient`` and ``FakeAcliClient`` enrichment. Hermetic integration tests always exercise ``FakeAcliClient``. Opt-in external tests exercise ``AcliClient`` against Jira. These assertions are their single verified-fake contract and check required keys plus JSON primitive types, never change-detecting values. Both tiers import this root helper through the ``tests/`` path.\tPASS\t122\t49\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_live_jira_confinement.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_live_jira_confinement.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_live_jira_confinement.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Fail when Jira-connected tests would run under an xdist scheduler that ignores their group. Only ``--dist loadgroup`` honors ``xdist_group``. ``load`` and ``worksteal`` scatter tests that share one eventually consistent Jira project. The guard fires only for a parallel run with Jira credentials, ``acli``, and collected group members, so credential-less CI remains unaffected. It stays outside ``conftest.py`` as a directly testable pure predicate.\tPASS\t200\t63\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_log_integrity.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_log_integrity.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_log_integrity.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Shared primitives that keep ``caplog`` assertions from passing on missing records. Capture depends on both ``rebar`` and ``rebar_reconciler`` parent loggers emitting and propagating to the root handler. Process-global ``propagate=False`` or a raised parent level can silently sever that path. Changing only the root level does not repair it. The conftest guard therefore fails at the source for propagation changes and restores legitimate entrypoint level changes after each test, preventing order-dependent vacuous assertions. Its self-test imports these exact helpers rather than a copy.\tPASS\t416\t83\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_log_integrity.py#D:restore_level\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_log_integrity.py#D:restore_level\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_log_integrity.py#D:restore_level\tpytest and maintainers of restore_level. Preserves Restore all shared-root levels and report whether any moved. In-process CLI and reconciler entrypoints legitimately pin their logger to WARNING. Only leaking that level is an error. Per-test restoration gives every later log assertion the same starting state regardless of execution order.\tPASS\t97\t42\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_nested_pytest.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_nested_pytest.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_nested_pytest.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Centralize nested pytest launches around a caller-owned ``--basetemp``. Hand-built children can clean another run's shared numbered temp root. Most callers use :func:`run_nested_pytest`. Import-convention tests intentionally invoke bare ``pytest`` with their own basetemp so ``python -m`` does not alter ``sys.path``, while ``pytester`` owns its temp root. The uniqueness guard recognizes ``python -m pytest``, pytest-bearing ``python -c``, and the console script structurally, enforcing the temp-root invariant rather than helper monopoly.\tPASS\t221\t70\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_nested_pytest.py#D:run_nested_pytest\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_nested_pytest.py#D:run_nested_pytest\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_nested_pytest.py#D:run_nested_pytest\tpytest and maintainers of run_nested_pytest. Preserves Run ``python -m pytest`` with a basetemp owned by *tmp_path*. Forward required *env* verbatim so deliberately minimal mappings stay minimal. Callers opt into ambient state with ``subprocess_env()``. Create the parent that pytest omits. Forward *timeout*, propagate ``TimeoutExpired``, apply no ``check``, and return the completed process unchanged.\tPASS\t153\t46\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_repo_root.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_repo_root.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_repo_root.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Find checkout-only test artifacts independently of package installation layout. Deriving the root from ``rebar.__file__`` fails for wheel installs because it points into site-packages. Test files always remain in the checkout, so walk upward from this helper to the nearest ancestor containing both ``pyproject.toml`` and ``hatch_build.py``. This also tolerates moving the helper between test directories.\tPASS\t169\t56\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_stall_remote.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_stall_remote.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_stall_remote.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Local fake Git remote for throughput-sensitive stall-abort tests. All fetch sites share two minimal HTTP modes. ``stall`` sends headers then no body, while ``dribble`` continuously sends bytes at a fixed rate. Their contrast proves the abort is keyed to stalled throughput rather than a shorter wall-clock timeout, which would kill both.\tPASS\t110\t51\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_subprocess_isolation.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_subprocess_isolation.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_subprocess_isolation.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Collection-time enforcement of unit-tier subprocess isolation. The per-worker ``REBAR_ROOT`` sandbox reaches children only through environment inheritance. Rebuilding ``env=`` can drop it and send a child into the shared checkout. ``scan_source`` AST-resolves imported spawn callees and returns hazards or report-only undecidable findings. ``unharnessed_subprocess_reason`` scopes hazards to collected items and formats the failure. Unresolvable external environment bindings never fail collection. Keeping the predicate outside ``conftest.py`` makes the implementation directly testable.\tPASS\t218\t69\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_topology_template.py#D:_assert_bare_repositories_pinned\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_topology_template.py#D:_assert_bare_repositories_pinned\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_topology_template.py#D:_assert_bare_repositories_pinned\tpytest and maintainers of _assert_bare_repositories_pinned. Preserves Reject topology copies containing a bare repository with unpinned upkeep. Detached post-push maintenance can repack while ``copytree`` and later tree scans walk the object store. Guarding this sole whole-topology copy point converts that race into a deterministic error naming every repository and missing pin, including future fixtures.\tPASS\t146\t47\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/_tree_scan.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/_tree_scan.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/_tree_scan.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Cache immutable Python-source tree scans for whole-tree policy oracles. Repeated ``rglob``/read/``ast.parse`` passes dominate the policy tier, especially under coverage. Parse each source root once per worker so all opted-in oracles share one result.\tPASS\t94\t36\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Repo-wide pytest isolation and configuration. Autouse guards keep tests in disposable roots. New checkout entries fail but remain untouched because snapshots cannot attribute concurrent writes, while session porcelain checks cover writes inside existing tracked directories. Unit and scripts tests also fail on network sockets unless explicitly marked ``allow_network``. Test filesystem writes belong under ``tmp_path`` or another sandbox.\tPASS\t170\t57\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#D:pytest_configure\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#D:pytest_configure\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#D:pytest_configure\tpytest and maintainers of pytest_configure. Preserves Fail below the declared Git floor before registering custom markers. Two-clone convergence requires ``merge-tree --write-tree`` and must never silently skip. Contributor docs and CI share the value in ``.github/git-version-floor.txt``.\tPASS\t66\t31\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#D:pytest_collection_modifyitems\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#D:pytest_collection_modifyitems\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#D:pytest_collection_modifyitems\tpytest and maintainers of pytest_collection_modifyitems. Preserves Enforce directory confinement and path-based collection markers. Mark everything under ``tests/external`` and fail if an external/billable item lives elsewhere, so the default marker expression excludes that entire tier. Also apply the reduced macOS ``platform_compat`` marker from its centralized path fragments.\tPASS\t110\t42\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#D:_is_coverage_artifact\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#D:_is_coverage_artifact\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#D:_is_coverage_artifact\tpytest and maintainers of _is_coverage_artifact. Preserves Recognize coverage.py data as framework output rather than test leaks. Under xdist, finished workers write ``.coverage.<host>.<pid>.<rand>`` before pytest-cov combines them. Another worker's per-test snapshot can observe that new file, so the guard excludes these gitignored plugin artifacts instead of failing or deleting them.\tPASS\t135\t47\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#D:_bound_review_bot_shutdown_drain\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#D:_bound_review_bot_shutdown_drain\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#D:_bound_review_bot_shutdown_drain\tpytest and maintainers of _bound_review_bot_shutdown_drain. Preserves Shorten review-bot draining and neutralize suite-wide hard process exits. A lifespan timer can call ``os._exit`` after its originating test and kill an unrelated xdist worker. Replacing that seam keeps arming logic exercised. Force-down tests install their own recorder afterward. Import remains optional because the default tier may lack FastAPI.\tPASS\t135\t49\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#D:_default_rebar_root_to_sandbox\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#D:_default_rebar_root_to_sandbox\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#D:_default_rebar_root_to_sandbox\tpytest and maintainers of _default_rebar_root_to_sandbox. Preserves Default repository and gate storage to a per-session sandbox. Otherwise an unset ``REBAR_ROOT`` resolves to the checkout and commands may mount the checkout's ``.tickets-tracker``, causing xdist leak failures. Later test monkeypatches or explicit deletion still win. ``REBAR_GATE_TMPDIR`` also isolates child admission tests from host operator slots while allowing narrower fixture overrides.\tPASS\t126\t51\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#D:_gate_source_attested_by_default\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#D:_gate_source_attested_by_default\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#D:_gate_source_attested_by_default\tpytest and maintainers of _gate_source_attested_by_default. Preserves Use an offline-safe immutable basis for code-reading gate tests. Production attests ``origin/main``, but disposable repos have no remote. ``HEAD`` preserves attested, signable snapshot semantics without fetching. The former local source allowed dirty reads and is intentionally unsignable. Consequently, drift fixtures must commit changes. Tests needing in-place reads explicitly select ``source=local`` and expect no signature. Existing environment or explicit arguments retain precedence.\tPASS\t232\t63\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#D:_identity_enforcement_off_by_default\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#D:_identity_enforcement_off_by_default\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#D:_identity_enforcement_off_by_default\tpytest and maintainers of _identity_enforcement_off_by_default. Preserves Unconditionally disable authenticated-authorship enforcement in the general suite. Ambient enforcement would make unsigned fixture writes fail. Dedicated identity tests pass an explicit subprocess environment, so their enabled value still wins in the child.\tPASS\t124\t33\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#D:_compaction_trigger_off_by_default\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#D:_compaction_trigger_off_by_default\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#D:_compaction_trigger_off_by_default\tpytest and maintainers of _compaction_trigger_off_by_default. Preserves Prevent detached compaction workers from escaping offline tests. Production's async trigger is correct, but a worker can outlive its test and race later writes to the same temporary store. Default to ``off``. Trigger-specific tests explicitly choose inline ``always`` or stubbed ``async``, and their value wins.\tPASS\t157\t45\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#D:_no_ambient_model_classes\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#D:_no_ambient_model_classes\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#D:_no_ambient_model_classes\tpytest and maintainers of _no_ambient_model_classes. Preserves Unconditionally remove ambient model-class field overrides from ordinary tests. ``REBAR_ROOT`` already isolates project config, but exported class models/providers/endpoints could retarget literal ladder expectations and create unrelated failures. Override-mechanism tests set their environment after this fixture, so their deliberate values still win.\tPASS\t190\t43\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:import _extra_guard\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:import _extra_guard\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:import _extra_guard\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves --- Optional-extra coverage guard (bug 599e-77da-29dd-482d) ---------------------- CI sets REBAR_REQUIRE_EXTRAS=1 so missing extras cannot silently skip test surfaces. The directly tested guard lives in _extra_guard. Conftest imports it before test modules load.\tPASS\t72\t30\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:_PLATFORM_COMPAT_PATH_FRAGMENTS\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:_PLATFORM_COMPAT_PATH_FRAGMENTS\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:_PLATFORM_COMPAT_PATH_FRAGMENTS\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Repo-relative path fragments select the reduced macOS compatibility suite. Linux runs the full suite. Slower macOS runners cover ``platform_compat`` plus integration for Darwin-specific locking, atomic rename, timeout-command, and Git-contention behavior. Path selection keeps the policy in one reviewable place instead of scattered file markers.\tPASS\t110\t44\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#C:pytest_collection_modifyitems:before:import _live_jira_confinement\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#C:pytest_collection_modifyitems:before:import _live_jira_confinement\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#C:pytest_collection_modifyitems:before:import _live_jira_confinement\tpytest and maintainers of pytest_collection_modifyitems. Preserves (c) Reject Jira-connected groups under schedulers that ignore xdist_group. The pure predicate is inert without Jira credentials. Raise UsageError because pytest.fail() from the xdist controller renders as an INTERNALERROR traceback instead of a clear remedy.\tPASS\t131\t36\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#C:pytest_collection_modifyitems:before:import _subprocess_isolation\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#C:pytest_collection_modifyitems:before:import _subprocess_isolation\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#C:pytest_collection_modifyitems:before:import _subprocess_isolation\tpytest and maintainers of pytest_collection_modifyitems. Preserves (d) Reject unit-tier children that escape inherited REBAR_ROOT through a hand-built env or shared-checkout cwd. The testable AST predicate lives outside conftest. Use UsageError, as above, so xdist presents the actionable message rather than an INTERNALERROR.\tPASS\t106\t36\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:_TOOLING_CACHE_ARTIFACTS\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:_TOOLING_CACHE_ARTIFACTS\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:_TOOLING_CACHE_ARTIFACTS\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Gitignored tool caches are framework output, not test-body leaks. Exempting the class is portable across pytest versions and CI providers, including runs that still materialize ``.pytest_cache`` with the cache provider disabled.\tPASS\t76\t31\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#C:_no_repo_root_leaks:before:pytest.fail\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#C:_no_repo_root_leaks:before:pytest.fail\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#C:_no_repo_root_leaks:before:pytest.fail\tpytest and maintainers of _no_repo_root_leaks. Preserves Report only. A before/after diff proves that an entry appeared, not which process wrote it. Concurrent Git, editors, and agents are indistinguishable from the test. timestamps and names cannot supply ownership. Never delete the entry, and tell the operator it remains for safe classification and cleanup.\tPASS\t136\t47\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:_REPORTED_FOREIGN_ENGINE\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:_REPORTED_FOREIGN_ENGINE\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:_REPORTED_FOREIGN_ENGINE\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves --- Canonical reconciler engine root (bug bd2d-3e31-31d9-4a66) -------------------- Non-editable installs contain checkout and site-packages engine copies, but a canonical ``rebar_reconciler.*`` key can bind only one. Mixing them gives tests module objects unlike those held by the code under test. The root guard inspects final import state, covering module assignment, imports, and package paths in every tier. It reports each foreign binding once so the introducing test fails rather than all later consumers.\tPASS\t177\t70\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:from _isolation import head\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:from _isolation import head\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:from _isolation import head\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves ── Repo-isolation guard (no test may commit to / mutate this checkout) ─────── Tests use disposable trackers. Git can walk upward from a non-repository fixture and commit to this checkout, while writes inside existing tracked directories evade the top-level leak guard. A per-test HEAD check attributes the first class. A session porcelain backstop catches the second. ``allow_repo_writes`` marks deliberate exceptions, and shared primitives reside in _isolation so self-tests exercise the production guard.\tPASS\t150\t68\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:import _log_integrity\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:import _log_integrity\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/conftest.py#C:<module>:before:import _log_integrity\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves ── caplog coverage integrity (bug 9ac2) ───────────────────────────────────── Empty caplog records make absence assertions pass vacuously. Capture for both ``rebar`` and ``rebar_reconciler`` depends on their parent logger emitting and propagating to the root. ``propagate=False`` severs that path. A raised parent level drops records before root-level adjustments can help. Propagation changes are never legitimate and fail the originating test. Entry points may legitimately raise their logger level, so that state is restored per test. Shared detection in _log_integrity keeps all tests order-independent and lets the guard's self-test exercise the same implementation.\tPASS\t343\t87\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\ntests/module_size_support.py#D:<module>\t88c90f8b5abf4a80be3b1289d7719d6e03e29684:tests/module_size_support.py#D:<module>\ta4796923df601c6ff6de2d832c9e755eae717d21:tests/module_size_support.py#D:<module>\tpytest collection and module maintainers. Preserves Single source for the CI module-size computation used by two test surfaces. The in-process contract and scc reconciliation tests share the gate's ``wc -l`` rule so it cannot drift between implementations. This helper lives at the deliberately importable ``tests/`` root. Cross-directory imports would depend on pytest's changing basedir behavior. Paths anchor to ``__file__`` so ``pytest`` and ``python -m pytest`` agree from any cwd.\tPASS\t172\t62\tPASS\tPASS\t/root@2026-09-10-resume\nRECEIPT_SUMMARY\trows=51\tbefore_words=8212\tafter_words=2549\tsemantic_pass=51\tbloat_pass=51\tdirectives_exact=51\tsha256=b3d1b513ed5139e02da99e9364075a3889ebb351f8d7769d303d4b753d2d8d98"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789052325144576001,"uuid":"3bd364ed-522d-4b47-a512-209eb75d0143"}